    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-01-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-01",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "Amplitude, frequency and phase",
        "or": "Amplitude, Frequency ଓ Phase"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "A sinusoidal signal repeats smoothly over time. Amplitude measures its peak size, frequency counts cycles per second, and phase describes its position within a cycle relative to a reference. For x(t)=A sin(2*pi*f*t+phi), time is in seconds, f is in Hz and phi is in radians. The period is T=1/f. A 100 Hz signal therefore repeats every 0.01 s. Some software fields require angular frequency rather than Hz: enter omega=2*pi*f rad/s. Changing amplitude does not itself change frequency. Always read the axis units before comparing waveforms.",
        "or": "Sinusoidal signal ସମୟ ସହିତ ପୁଣିପୁଣି ସମାନ ଭାବରେ ବଦଳେ। Amplitude ଏହାର ସର୍ବାଧିକ ଆକାର, Frequency ଏକ ସେକେଣ୍ଡରେ କେତେ cycle ହୁଏ, ଏବଂ Phase ଏକ reference ସହିତ cycle ର ସ୍ଥିତି ଦର୍ଶାଏ। Period T=1/f। 100 Hz signal ର Period 0.01 s। Simulink ର time-based Sine Wave block ରେ Frequency ପାଇଁ 2*pi*f rad/s ଦେବାକୁ ପଡ଼େ। Amplitude ବଦଳିଲେ Frequency ଆପେଆପେ ବଦଳେ ନାହିଁ। Waveform ତୁଳନା ପୂର୍ବରୁ axis ର unit ଦେଖନ୍ତୁ।"
      },
      "termIds": [
        "T-AM-01-1",
        "T-AM-01-2",
        "T-AM-01-3"
      ],
